<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Adibo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1896">1896</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Adibo was fought in 1896 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yendi">Yendi</a>, in what is now northern Ghana, between German colonial forces advancing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togo">Togo</a> and the army of the Dagomba kingdom of Dagbon. The Germans, with modern rifles, defeated the Dagomba cavalry and then burned Yendi. In 1899 an Anglo-German agreement divided Dagbon between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> and German Togoland.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1896 Valentin von Massow, Gruner and Gaston Thierry met the Dagomba at the <b>Battle of Adibo</b>: about 7,000 poorly equipped Dagomba rushed with bows and arrows at 100 well-armed Germans, and it was a massacre.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-dagbon">Kingdom of Dagbon · Military</a></li></ul></section>
